Package: secubox-photoprism
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends}, secubox-core (>= 1.5.39~), python3-uvicorn | python3-pip,
 lxc, lxc-templates, nftables, openssl, python3-yaml
Recommends: secubox-auth
Description: PhotoPrism photo management for SecuBox (native LXC)
 SecuBox module for a PhotoPrism photo server installed natively (official
 build from dl.photoprism.app) inside a dedicated Debian LXC, running as its
 own unprivileged user. No podman, no docker. `photoprismctl install`
 provisions the LXC on demand; the host dashboard daemon stays lightweight
 and always reachable.
 .
 Photos live on /data/shared/photos, also mounted by Nextcloud as the
 "PhotoLibrary" external storage — phone → Nextcloud → /data/shared/photos →
 PhotoPrism originals (indexed by a 15-min timer, since PhotoPrism's built-in
 auto-index only fires for its own UI uploads).
 .
 Features:
  - LXC lifecycle via photoprismctl (install/update/status/start/stop/restart/index/import)
  - Public nginx vhost (:9080 → LXC :2342) behind sbxwaf inspection
  - AI-powered face recognition, library indexing, album management
  - Import workflow + Nextcloud photo integration
  - CRT-light P31 phosphor theme
 .
 Provides FastAPI backend on /api/v1/photoprism/ via Unix socket.
